## 6. Research Sequence

The research should proceed in controlled stages:

```text
EA095-M1-BASELINE-001
        ↓
Timeframe Evaluation
        ↓
ATR Multiplier Evaluation
        ↓
Entry Confirmation Evaluation
        ↓
Trading Session Evaluation
        ↓
BUY vs SELL Evaluation
        ↓
Exit Management Evaluation
        ↓
Longer Historical Test
        ↓
Out-of-Sample Validation
        ↓
Robustness Testing
        ↓
Forward Testing
```

Only one major strategy component should be changed in each controlled experiment.

---

## 7. Research Rules

### Rule 1 — Preserve the baseline

The baseline EA must remain unchanged.

### Rule 2 — One major variable at a time

Each experiment should isolate one strategy component.

### Rule 3 — No broad optimization at the beginning

Do not optimize multiple parameters simultaneously before understanding which component affects performance.

### Rule 4 — Compare against baseline

Every experiment must be compared with:

`EA095-M1-BASELINE-001`

### Rule 5 — Separate discovery from validation

A result found on the same historical data used for research should not automatically be considered validated.

### Rule 6 — No live deployment from baseline

The current baseline is not production-ready.

---

## 8. Current Research Conclusion

EA-095_ATR_Stretch_2_0 baseline does not currently show a profitable trading edge under the tested configuration.

The baseline remains useful as a controlled reference point.

The next research objective should be to determine whether the weakness comes from:

1. the M1 timeframe;
2. the ATR stretch threshold;
3. the entry confirmation;
4. trading-session effects;
5. directional asymmetry between BUY and SELL;
6. or the exit-management model.

No conclusion should be drawn about the entire strategy family until these components have been tested independently.
